  <ctml:notes>Saint Charbel Chess Cup IV Masters, 3-9 September 2026: a 10-player single round robin (9 rounds, 45 games) with the possibility of fulfilling GM and IM norms. Time control: 90 minutes with 30 second increment from move 1 (FIDE standard rated). Location: Morshyn, Lviv Oblast, Ukraine, at the Saint Charbel Hotel&amp;Spa. Tournament director: Prystay, Mykola (UKR); Chief Arbiter: Ilnitskyy, Ivan (UKR, FA); Deputy Chief Arbiter: Cherniak, Olena (UKR, FA). Pairing program: Swiss-Manager from Heinz Herzog. Final standings: 1 Dubnevych 6.5/9, 2 Miezis 5.5/9, 3 Zilka 5.5/9, 4 Dyachuk 5/9, 5 Pankiv 4.5/9, 6 Tulchynskyi 4.5/9, 7 Karvatskyi 4/9, 8 Golubev 4/9, 9 Povshednyi 4/9, 10 Gronn 1.5/9. Tiebreak order: Sonneborn-Berger. Average rating: 2415. Identity is by FIDE id. ECO codes and opening names from the Lichess broadcast PGN. Every ply has a clock value (from broadcast relay). Engine evaluations present in PGN comments are not carried into CTML. Uses the CTML 2.1 model (participant/placement). Round schedule: R1 Sep 3, R2-R3 Sep 4, R4 Sep 5, R5 Sep 6, R6 Sep 7, R7-R8 Sep 8, R9 Sep 9.</ctml:notes>
